{"id":"bayraktar-tb2","slug":"bayraktar-tb2","name":"Bayraktar TB2 / Bayraktar TB2T-AI","aliases":["TB2 drone","TB-2 drone","Bayraktar-TB2","Bayraktar TB2","Bayraktar TB-2","Bayraktar drone","Bayraktar TB2 drone","Baykar Bayraktar TB2"],"kind":"aircraft","category":"drones","subcategory":"Turkish unmanned combat aerial vehicle","description":"Bayraktar TB2 is a family of medium-altitude long-endurance (MALE) unmanned combat aerial vehicles (UCAV) capable of remotely controlled or autonomous flight operations. It is manufactured by the Turkish company Baykar for the Turkish Armed Forces and export markets. The aircraft are monitored and controlled by an aircrew in a ground control station, including weapons employment. The development of the UAV has been largely credited to Selçuk Bayraktar, a former MIT graduate student along with his brother Haluk Bayraktar. It is the first UCAV in the world to successfully perform a barrel roll and an autonomous spin recovery maneuver. It is the most produced and export-successful UCAV in the world. Baykar has a production capacity of 250 Bayraktar TB2s per year and is aiming to increase the production capacity to 500 per year.","development":"The development of the Bayraktar TB2 was spurred by a U.S. ban on exports of armed unmanned aircraft to Turkey due to concerns that they would be used against PKK groups inside and outside Turkey.\nBaykar started developing a new combat tactical aerial vehicle system at the request of the Presidency of Defense Industries, after the experiences of its first tactical UAV, the Bayraktar Çaldıran or Bayraktar TB1, delivered to the Turkish army in 2011. The Bayraktar TB2 made its maiden flight in August 2014. On 18 December 2015, a video was published of a test firing of a missile from the Bayraktar TB2, a result of a collaboration with Roketsan. Roketsan's MAM and TUBITAK-SAGE's BOZOK laser-guided bombs were tested for the first time.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"General","items":[{"label":"First Flight","value":"2014"},{"label":"Primary User","value":"Turkey"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"Baykar"},{"label":"Number Built","value":">800"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"Turkey"},{"label":"Status","value":"In service"}]}],"specIndex":{"First Flight":"2014","Primary User":"Turkey","Manufacturer":"Baykar","Number Built":">800","Origin":"Turkey","Status":"In service"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Bayraktar_TB2_Runway.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayraktar_TB2_Runway.jpg","width":3129,"height":1305,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Bayhaluk"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Bayraktar_TB2_Runway.jpg/330px-Bayraktar_TB2_Runway.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Bayraktar_TB2_Ground.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayraktar_TB2_Ground.jpg","width":5312,"height":2988,"caption":"Bayraktar TB2 Ground","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Bayhaluk"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/BayraktarTB2_Teknofest2019_%282%29.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BayraktarTB2_Teknofest2019_(2).jpg","width":2934,"height":4430,"caption":"Unmanned aerial vehicle TB2 of Bayraktar at Teknofest 2019","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"CeeGee"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/Roketsan_MAM-L_Mini_Ak%C4%B1ll%C4%B1_M%C3%BChimmat%2C_Teknofest_2019.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roketsan_MAM-L_Mini_Ak%C4%B1ll%C4%B1_M%C3%BChimmat,_Teknofest_2019.jpg","width":3862,"height":2350,"caption":"Roketsan MAM-L Mini Akıllı Mühimmat, Tek